%U A394412 40611135172608000,1084135280836608000,30641760555614208000,917082411982184448000,31737206696664268800000
%N A394412 Number of homomorphisms from the figure-eight knot group to the symmetric group S_n.
%C A394412 For an n-sheeted covering of the figure-eight knot complement, following a loop permutes the n points above a chosen basepoint. After labeling these points 1,...,n, the resulting permutations form a homomorphism G -> S_n, and every such homomorphism arises in this way. The cover may be disconnected; the orbits of the permutation action are its connected components.
%C A394412 The transitive homomorphisms therefore describe connected covers. The recurrence in the Formula section recovers s(n), the number of index-n subgroups of G, from a(n); equivalently, s(n) counts connected n-sheeted covers with a chosen point over the basepoint. Thus a(n) records the finite-cover, or subgroup-growth, data of the figure-eight knot group.
%C A394412 Using the standard two-generator presentation G = <x,y | y*x*y^(-1)*x*y = x*y*x^(-1)*y*x>, a homomorphism is determined by the images X,Y in S_n of the two generators, subject to the relation displayed in the Formula section.
%H A394412 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A394412/b394412.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..24</a>
%H A394412 M. Culler, N. Dunfield, M. Goerner, et al., <a href="https://github.com/3-manifolds/low_index/tree/d42e89864272fe3f378228b3a227fee833496a70">low_index: low-index subgroup enumeration, commit d42e89864272fe3f378228b3a227fee833496a70</a>.
%H A394412 M. Deraux and E. Falbel, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.7096">Complex hyperbolic geometry of the figure-eight knot</a>, Geometry & Topology 19 (2015), 237-293. See Section 3, equation (8), for a presentation of the figure-eight knot group.
%H A394412 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A394412/a394412.cpp.txt">C++20 program for computing the terms</a>.
%H A394412 A. Hatcher, <a href="https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATch1.3rev.pdf">Algebraic Topology, Chapter 1, Section 1.3: Covering Spaces</a>, Cambridge University Press, 2002.
%F A394412 a(n) = Card({(X,Y) in S_n^2 : Y*X*Y^(-1)*X*Y = X*Y*X^(-1)*Y*X}).
%F A394412 s(k) = Sum_{rho in R_k} k/|Aut_G(rho)|, where R_k is a set of representatives of the transitive G-actions of degree k up to isomorphism.
%F A394412 If F(0)=1, then n*F(n)=Sum_{k=1..n} s(k)*F(n-k) and a(n)=n!*F(n).
%e A394412 For n=2, let e be the identity and t=(1,2). Since S_2 is abelian and every element is its own inverse, the relation reduces to X=Y. Hence the two homomorphisms are (X,Y)=(e,e) and (t,t). The first fixes both sheet labels and gives the disconnected trivial double cover of the figure-eight knot complement; the second swaps the labels around either generator and gives its connected two-sheeted cyclic cover. Therefore a(2)=2.
%o A394412 (C++) // Save the linked source as figure8.cpp. Compile: g++ -std=c++20 -O3 -DNDEBUG -pthread figure8.cpp -o figure8. Run: ./figure8 24 100 certificate.tsv optimized.
%Y A394412 Cf. A239837 and A255515 (related permutation-relation counts), A061207 (index-n subgroups of the trefoil knot group), A394222 (Fox colorings of the figure-eight knot).
